# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository and on checkout.
# Ends the CRLF churn that polluted whole-file diffs (editor saves and
# MSYS sed both flipped endings on and off — see the persistence
# refactor slices, 2026-09-12). Binary detection stays automatic.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-braces for the binary assets that live next to the sources.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.onnx binary
*.npy binary
*.dll binary
*.glb binary
*.vrm binary
*.fbx binary
*.exr binary
*.hdr binary
*.spv binary

# Vendored crates are snapshots of upstream releases plus the documented
# local patch (docs/realsense-build.md). EOL normalization would make
# the vendored copy diverge from upstream byte-for-byte and break the
# "keep the diff minimal to ease rebasing" contract — including the
# upstream-shipped prebuilt bindings, which use CRLF.
vendor/** -text
